joinly v0.5.4 files, changed by switchboard (#713, DESIGN.md section 52.5)

server.py and kokoro.py are copies of two files of joinly v0.5.4
(https://github.com/joinly-ai/joinly, tag v0.5.4), which is MIT licensed:
Copyright (c) 2025 Dominik Brockmann, Johannes Dittrich, Fynn Aurand. The licence is
at the top of each file, as it requires. switchboard is not affiliated with joinly.

They are mounted read-only over the image's own copies, pinned by sha256 (docs/DEPLOY.md,
"A meeting bot"), until a joinly release lets `speak_text` take a voice.

What changed from v0.5.4

  joinly/server.py
    - `speak_text` takes an optional `voice` (a Kokoro voice name: a-z, 0-9 and _, 1 to 32
      characters), for that call of the tool only.
    - It sets the voice for the length of the call and clears it afterwards.
    - When Kokoro did not know the voice, the answer reads "Finished speaking. The voice was
      not found, so the session's voice was used." instead of "Finished speaking."

  joinly/services/tts/kokoro.py
    - A context variable holds the voice of the line being spoken. `_tts` reads it and falls
      back to the session's voice (`tts_args`) when it is unset or Kokoro has no such voice.

Both files are also formatted with this repository's ruff settings, so its lint passes (line
breaks and an import order only). Without a `voice`, joinly behaves as v0.5.4.
The same two files are in plugins/claude/meeting/joinly/ and plugins/codex/meeting/joinly/;
tests/unit/test_joinly_voice_patch.py keeps the three copies identical.
